TITLE: SYS-ARI-001 · Calculate with string numbers

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-ARI-001
VERSION: 1
TITLE: Calculate with string numbers
STATEMENT: >>>
When a client sends a calculation request with two valid string numbers and
one of the operations addition, subtraction, multiplication or division, the
service **shall** respond with the result of that operation as a string
number.
<<<
KIND: functional
STATUS: draft
PRIORITY: high
SAFETY: QM
RELEASE: 1.0.0
VERIFICATION: test
VERIF_LEVELS: system
TAGS: arithmetic, api
SOURCE: Stakeholder request, 2026-11-18
OWNER: msforenter090
CREATED: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
RATIONALE: >>>
Clients need to calculate with numbers that are too long or too precise for
the number types of their own platforms (for example 64-bit integers or
floating point). Passing numbers as strings keeps every digit.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
- The service keeps no state between requests. Nothing is stored, and there
  is no user interface; the HTTP API is the only interface.
- The request and response format and the exact rules per operation are
  defined at software level. See child requirements REQ-API-001 and
  REQ-ARI-001 to REQ-ARI-004.
- Terms *client*, *service*, *calculation request*, *operand* and *string
  number* are defined in the glossary.
<<<
